Safety section	UNKNOWN STEP	**Current candidate: `12a057424`.** The [ordinary-reader cleanup review](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/pull/133#pullrequestreview-5366098967) is addressed: reproduced callback-dependent cleanup joins and leased-reader self-disposal leaks now have scoped fixes, permanent guards, independent validation and two further actual-before/fixed proofs. **Final qualification is pending the new hosted matrix.** The fresh exact-source benchmark is complete and reported below, with independent calculation review underway. The preceding `f95` run failed two Windows tests: an ARM64 native-crash fixture read sharing violation and an x64 pinned-writer output timeout. Their original causes remain unknown. Failure capture and progress oracles are strengthened without retries or production timing changes; original failures and the missing ARM fixture limitation remain explicit.
